    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The `SettingWithCopyWarning` is triggered when you modify a subset of a DataFrame that was passed to you as a copy, rather than a view. This warning occurs because most DataFrame assignments in Python default to returning a view of the original DataFrame. To fix this, you need to ensure you are working with a copy of the DataFrame, either by calling `.copy()` on the original DataFrame or by assigning the subset to a temporary variable using `.copy()`. \n\nFor example, to avoid the warning: `temp_df = df_subset.copy()` and then perform the desired operations on `temp_df`. Alternatively, if you are certain you are working with a view of the original DataFrame, you can suppress the warning with `warnings.filterwarnings('ignore', category=RuntimeWarning, module='pandas')`.",
